From 01defee938603fcd95517d1d6c3df6459afd6de1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:14:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [ActiveAE] Add a setting for what the volume controls

The volume and mute scale Kodi's own audio only, which leaves other
programs on the same output device at their own level.

Add a Volume control setting with the choices Kodi's audio, the default,
and Output device, shown when the selected device has a volume control.
With Output device the engine sets the device's volume and mute through
the sink factory whenever they change, whether its sink is open or not,
and leaves Kodi's samples unscaled. The device keeps its own volume
until Kodi has restored its saved one, so it never jumps to full volume
at start-up.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
